  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the mean of the differences between outcomes and a reference value (here, zero), weighted by their probabilities—essentially expected value relative to reference. The individual did not mention or appear to calculate such differences or their probabilistic weighting. Instead, they focused on the perceived similarity in probabilities and then compared the outcome amounts directly, favoring the one they believed had a higher potential gain (though they misidentified which lottery that was). There is no evidence that the individual used a reference value or computed mean differences. The justification is based on a simple dominance heuristic (similar chances, pick higher outcome), not on the structured probabilistic evaluation required by the decision reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
